+**Pitfalls:**
+*   **Background Influence:** Background voxels (e.g., air) have high occurrence and can negatively influence the map if included in training. They should be removed via region growing from exterior seeds if they do not carry useful information [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Homogeneous Region Dominance:** Without the modified neighborhood function ($nf2$), large homogeneous regions of the volume would dominate the map, while important regions with fewer voxels (signatures far from their winner cells) would be badly represented [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Information Loss:** Dimensional reduction causes loss and distortion of information, making accurate quantitative analysis impossible. The method is suitable only for qualitative aspects like shape and dissimilarity [S1].
+*   **Normal Computation:** Precomputed normals cannot be used for multivariate data sets because the attributes lack a clear physical meaning for normal orientation [S1].
 
